{"id": "EUVD-2026-101866", "enisaUuid": "e9a68853-9628-3634-b4da-e620545df3bc", "description": "renameat(2) did not enforce FD_RESOLVE_BENEATH on its directory arguments.  A jailed process could rename a directory relative to a restricted descriptor, then escape the jail root via fchdir(2).  This requires the directory to reside on a filesystem that is also reachable from the jail's root.\n\nA process in a jail that has received a directory file descriptor from another jail can use these techniques to escape the jail's filesystem root restriction.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T06:46:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:30:32", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://security.freebsd.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-26:66.jail.asc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-crp4-cfvg-6vr3", "CVE-2026-101305"], "assigner": "freebsd", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "46d63838-b06d-37ce-979f-7049372e8dd9", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.0-RELEASE <p14"}, {"id": "755b5fca-6665-37c6-8148-9b47489a8642", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.5-RELEASE <p1"}, {"id": "83a19d65-2975-3b73-bcea-ff5e4bebee2d", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "14.4-RELEASE <p10"}, {"id": "aeb912dc-d1f6-3e35-b845-949447f9cbb2", "product": {"name": "FreeBSD", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}, "product_version": "15.1-RELEASE <p4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5c634edf-f03a-3a81-833f-63fe66be7daf", "vendor": {"name": "FreeBSD"}}], "isExploited": false}